@startuml
title ARC-1155 MultiToken wired to CMTATAztecAuthMultiToken — the hook carries the id

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 260

actor Holder
box "Client side — proved on the holder's device" #F4F8FC
participant "MultiToken (aztec-standards)\ntransfer_private_to_private(from, to, id, amount, nonce)\nburn_private(from, id, amount, nonce)" as Tok
participant "CMTATAztecAuthMultiToken\nauthorize_private(from, id, amount, selector)" as Auth
participant "Public state\n(historical read at the anchor block)" as PS
end box
box "Sequencer — public phase of the same transaction" #FFF8E8
participant "CMTATAztecAuthMultiToken\n_require_lifecycle_allows(is_burn)\nonly_self" as AuthPub
end box

Holder -> Tok : transfer_private_to_private / burn_private
Tok -> Tok : authwit check (authorize_once)
Tok -> Auth : self.call(auth_contract.authorize_private(from, id, amount, selector))
note over Tok, Auth
  Same ARC-403 shape plus the token id. The id stays in the private domain:
  the contract accepts it and ignores it — pause, deactivation, freeze and the
  lists apply to every id alike. It is never forwarded to the public half.
end note

group Rules evaluated in private — DelayedPublicMutable, 360 s to bite
  Auth -> PS : is_frozen(from)
  Auth -> Auth : assert not frozen
  Auth -> PS : operations flag, list entry of from
  Auth -> Auth : blacklist / whitelist check on from
end

Auth -> Auth : is_burn = selector ∈ {burn_private 0x3198d2a7, burn_public 0x1d8b2815}\n(the id-bearing signatures, so different values from AIP-20)
Auth -> AuthPub : enqueue_self _require_lifecycle_allows(is_burn)
Auth --> Tok : ok
Tok -> Tok : nullify from's notes of `id`, create change note\n(transfer: recipient note for `to`)

== Public phase ==
AuthPub -> AuthPub : is_burn ? assert not deactivated\n        : assert not paused
alt refused
  AuthPub --> Holder : revert — the whole transaction fails
end

@enduml
